OL,3,CSolar eclipse wows Cumbria while
OL,4,Csouthern Scotland left in the shade
OL,6,FPeople across our region looked to the
OL,7,Fskies last night to try and catch a
OL,8,Fglimpse of the once-in-a-generation
OL,9,Fsolar eclipse.
OL,11,FMore than 90% of the sun was obscured
OL,12,Fby the moon between about 6pm and
OL,13,F8.15pm on Wednesday (12 August) -
OL,14,Fthat's the most it has been blocked
OL,15,Ffor those in the UK since the total
OL,16,Feclipse in 1999.
OL,18,FIn Dumfries, the peak eclipse happened
OL,19,Fat 7:07pm, in Galashiels at 7:06pm,
OL,20,Fwhile in Kendal the peak eclipse was
OL,21,Fseen at 7.08pm.
